The ReActEngine class is internal and some types like FunctionView are missing or not found in the expected path. Also, the _reActFunction field is private and not virtual, so I cannot override it for mocking. The same applies to GetAvailableFunctions and ParseResult methods which are not visible or virtual.

I will try to write a test that mocks ILogger and calls GetNextStepAsync via reflection or by creating a minimal test that exercises the logging call by passing a single function with no parameters to trigger the LogDebug call on line 157. I will also try to create a minimal Kernel and KernelArguments mocks.

I will submit a test that uses Moq to mock ILogger and KernelFunction and verifies the LogDebug call on the logger. I will not try to override or subclass ReActEngine but will test the method as is, focusing on the logging behavior.

